"{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.38\",\n  \"title\": \"The Indus Script and Economics.\",\n  \"authors\": \"Rajesh P. N. Rao\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.38\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2018-08-13T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.38\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 3,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Archaeopress Publishing Ltd', 'container_title': 'Walking with the Unicorn: Social Organization and Material Culture in Ancient South Asia', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '518-525', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1038/npre.2008.1900.1\",\n  \"title\": \"New Evidence for Early Silk in the Indus Civilization\",\n  \"authors\": \"Irene Good; Jonathan Mark Kenoyer; Richard Meadow\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title><jats:p>Silk is an important economic fiber, and is generally considered to have been the exclusive cultural heritage of China. Silk weaving is evident from the Shang period, though the earliest evidence for silk textiles in ancient China dates to more than a millennium earlier. New study of fibers from Harappan bronze artifacts reveals surprising early evidence for knowledge of silkworking in South Asia, the earliest evidence in the world for any silk outside China, and roughly contemporaneous with the earliest Chinese evidence for silk. This important new finding brings into question the traditional historical notion of sericulture as being an exclusively Chinese invention.</jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1038/npre.2008.1900.1\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2008-05-23T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/npre.2008.1900.1.pdf\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1038/npre.2008.1900.1\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 3,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Springer Science and Business Media LLC', 'container_title': 'Nature Precedings', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': ['1756-0357'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '297', 'prefix': '10.1038'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.9\",\n  \"title\": \"The Indus Valley Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.9\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2015-02-06T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.9\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Archaeopress Publishing Ltd', 'container_title': 'The Archaeology and Epigraphy of Indus Writing', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '4-12', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.14\",\n  \"title\": \"Proto-Dravidian and the Indus Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.14\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2015-02-06T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.14\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Archaeopress Publishing Ltd', 'container_title': 'The Archaeology and Epigraphy of Indus Writing', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '77-99', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.13\",\n  \"title\": \"Numerals in the Indus Script and their Uses\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.13\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2015-02-06T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.13\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Archaeopress Publishing Ltd', 'container_title': 'The Archaeology and Epigraphy of Indus Writing', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '66-76', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1525/aa.1996.98.1.02a00470\",\n  \"title\": \"<i>Deciphering the Indus Script.</i> Asko Parpola\",\n  \"authors\": \"Jonathan Mark Kenoyer\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1525/aa.1996.98.1.02a00470\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1996-03-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1525/aa.1996.98.1.02a00470\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Wiley', 'container_title': 'American Anthropologist', 'volume': '98', 'issue': '1', 'page': '198-199', 'issn': ['0002-7294', '1548-1433'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '311', 'prefix': '10.1111'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1075/wll.1.2.12bri\",\n  \"title\": \"Review of Possehl (1996): Indus age: The writing system\",\n  \"authors\": \"William Bright\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1075/wll.1.2.12bri\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1998-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1075/wll.1.2.12bri\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'John Benjamins Publishing Company', 'container_title': 'Written Language &amp; Literacy', 'volume': '1', 'issue': '2', 'page': '272-275', 'issn': ['1387-6732', '1570-6001'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '1757', 'prefix': '10.1075'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.26\",\n  \"title\": \"Toponyms, Directions and Tribal Names in the Indus Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"Iravatham Mahadevan; M. V. Bhaskar\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.26\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2018-08-13T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.26\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 1,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Archaeopress Publishing Ltd', 'container_title': 'Walking with the Unicorn: Social Organization and Material Culture in Ancient South Asia', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '359-376', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.22\",\n  \"title\": \"The Size of Indus Seals and its Significance\",\n  \"authors\": \"Ayumu Konasukawa; Manabu Koiso\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.22\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2018-08-13T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctv19vbgkc.22\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 2,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Archaeopress Publishing Ltd', 'container_title': 'Walking with the Unicorn: Social Organization and Material Culture in Ancient South Asia', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '292-317', 'issn': [], 'isbn': ['9781784919184'], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1111/j.1475-4754.2008.00454.x\",\n  \"title\": \"NEW EVIDENCE FOR EARLY SILK IN THE INDUS CIVILIZATION*\",\n  \"authors\": \"I. L. GOOD; J. M. KENOYER; R. H. MEADOW\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:p> <jats:italic>Silk is an important economic fibre, and is generally considered to have been the exclusive cultural heritage of China. Silk weaving is evident from the Shang period </jats:italic>c. <jats:italic>1600–1045 <jats:sc>bc</jats:sc>, though the earliest evidence for silk textiles in ancient China may date to as much as a millennium earlier. Recent microscopic analysis of archaeological thread fragments found inside copper‐alloy ornaments from Harappa and steatite beads from Chanhu‐daro, two important Indus sites, have yielded silk fibres, dating to </jats:italic>c. <jats:italic>2450–2000 <jats:sc>bc</jats:sc>. This study offers the earliest evidence in the world for any silk outside China, and is roughly contemporaneous with the earliest Chinese evidence for silk. This important new finding brings into question the traditional historical notion of sericulture as being an exclusively Chinese invention.</jats:italic></jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1111/j.1475-4754.2008.00454.x\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2009-05-05T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1475-4754.2008.00454.x\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 76,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Wiley', 'container_title': 'Archaeometry', 'volume': '51', 'issue': '3', 'page': '457-466', 'issn': ['0003-813X', '1475-4754'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '311', 'prefix': '10.1111'}\"\n}"
